      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Section 2. Bereavement Leave for Domestic Partners\nContinued. Any City employee who has registered his or her domestic partnership in accordance with the provisions of Executive Order No. 48, dated January 7, 1993, shall be entitled to bereavement leave in the event of the death of a domestic partner, or the death of a parent or child of such domestic partner, or the death of a relative of such domestic partner residing in the household. Such leave shall be afforded in accordance with existing rules and the terms of that Order. All \"Affidavits of Domestic Partnership for Bereavement Leave\" which were previously filed in accordance with prior Executive Order",
